  "description": "And A Recent Stock Up 5% ... Will The Trend Continue? - 13 February 2025",
  "body_html": "<p>This episode of Midweek Movers was fairly simple putting the bottom 5 stocks down. But the top 3 were pretty difficult to sort which had the most potential. We had a few “Recession proof” stocks such as T-Mobile and AT&amp;T to review. Communication stocks are often labeled as “recession proof” with the notion people will still use their phones and communicate even in a recession. Few will turn off their service. We also reviewed a stock we picked up yesterday that has surpassed 5% in a day, at the time of this video. </p><p>Please note that anything can change in a moment. We focus on consistent repeatable strategy, minimize risk and locking profits. As always, these are just my thoughts and opinions. If you have any questions feel free to reach out in the chat. Thanks for stopping by! 👍</p><div class=\"community-chat\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://open.substack.com/pub/tjstocks/chat?utm_source=chat_embed&quot;,&quot;subdomain&quot;:&quot;tjstocks&quot;,&quot;pub&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:3537822,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Timothy’s StockTok&quot;,&quot;author_name&quot;:&quot;StockTok&quot;,&quot;author_photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa4c61c40-9364-4166-877a-b0163fb9610d_854x854.png&quot;}}\" data-component-name=\"CommunityChatRenderPlaceholder\"></div>",
  "has_dynamic_content": false,
  "truncated_body_text": "This episode of Midweek Movers was fairly simple putting the bottom 5 stocks down. But the top 3 were pretty difficult to sort which had the most potential. We had a few “Recession proof” stocks such as T-Mobile and AT&T to review. Communication stocks are often labeled as “recession proof” with the notion people will still use their phones and communicate even in a recession. Few will turn off their service. We also reviewed a stock we picked up yesterday that has surpassed 5% in a day, at the time of this video.",
